- $ \lambda $ is the average wavelength of the light (in Å),
- $ \Delta N $ is the number of fringe cycles observed,
- $ d $ is the distance the mirror moves (in Å),
- $ \Delta \lambda $ is the separation between the two wavelengths (in Å).

